From: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pptpd: keep control and PPP process lifetimes owned

Track every controller, including delegate mode, and retire controllers
and the broadcast relay before exit. Keep
PPP in its original child process and reap it before releasing control.

Adopt descendants on forced controller exit and retain an inherited
exclusive instance lock through PPP and its scripts. A replacement cannot
accept clients while the old native owners remain, even if procd's
shutdown deadline forces the manager to exit. Lock acquisition failure
is reported before creating a relay or listener.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Bogdan Mircea <mirceapetrebogdan@gmail.com>
